53
00:05:12,302 --> 00:05:16,260
So anything left unclear then gets filled in using its own assumptions.

54
00:05:16,846 --> 00:05:21,476
And to see what that looks like, I'm going to start with a deliberately vague prompt like this.

55
00:05:21,934 --> 00:05:25,764
Build a task management app. That's it. Build the task management app.

56
00:05:25,856 --> 00:05:26,372
One sentence.

57
00:05:26,766 --> 00:05:28,656
The prompt explains the general idea, but nothing else.

58
00:05:28,736 --> 00:05:37,696
It doesn't say what information each task should contain, how tasks should be organized, what actions the user should be able to perform, or even what the app should look like.

59
00:05:38,126 --> 00:05:41,616
So base 44 has to make all of those decisions on its own.

60
00:05:41,934 --> 00:05:47,012
So the result will likely be a generic task manager based on familiar defaults.

61
00:05:47,310 --> 00:05:54,656
And yeah, the app may still be usable, but it could leave out features we expected or include things we never even asked for.

62
00:05:54,830 --> 00:06:04,256
And then getting it closer to the original idea would require one correction after another, and then each new prompt just adds more time to a result

63
00:06:04,416 --> 00:06:07,204
that could have been much more accurate from the very beginning.

64
00:06:07,630 --> 00:06:12,836
