72
00:06:54,830 --> 00:06:59,536
Use a clean minimal design with a white background and blue accent color.

73
00:06:59,616 --> 00:07:03,812
No authentication, no categories, and no team features yet.

74
00:07:04,366 --> 00:07:16,256
So now this version gives base44 a much clearer target it knows what information belongs to each task, how the list should be organized, and what should happen when a task is completed.

75
00:07:16,526 --> 00:07:21,828
It also knows the design direction and which features should not be added, not yet.

76
00:07:22,222 --> 00:07:25,056
Now, in this new version here, the priorities are already included.

77
00:07:25,326 --> 00:07:33,828
Pie priority tasks appear at the top, due dates are part of the task form, and completed tasks move to the bottom with a strike through.

78
00:07:34,158 --> 00:07:43,076
Now, the white background here and the blue accents also match the design that we asked for, rather than whatever default style base 44 might have chosen.

79
00:07:43,406 --> 00:07:52,804
Now the first result may have given us a starting point, okay, but the structured prompt though gets us much closer to the intended app in a single generation.

80
00:07:53,230 --> 00:08:01,860
Spending a few, just a few extra minutes here deciding what the app should do and how it should behave can actually prevent 10 follow-up prompts later.

81
00:08:02,254 --> 00:08:11,332
A first build that is already close to the goal just gives us more time to improve the app rather than correcting decisions we could have made from the very beginning.

82
00:08:11,616 --> 00:08:19,216
Authentication is one of those features that seems easy to leave until later, and you may want to finish the app first to make sure everything works

83
00:08:19,376 --> 00:08:22,660
and to deal with accounts once the product is nearly ready.

84
00:08:23,054 --> 00:08:33,060
