And then let's go ahead and log out, create a second account, and then add a different task. Now it's important here to test switching between these two accounts.

102
00:10:26,352 --> 00:10:34,084
The first user should only see the task created under the first account, while the second user, again, should only see their own task.

103
00:10:34,478 --> 00:10:39,844
Now both accounts can use the same app, yes, but their data should remain completely separate.

104
00:10:40,238 --> 00:10:48,100
Adding authentication at this stage now means every feature we build next can then use the logged in user from the very beginning.

105
00:10:48,558 --> 00:10:58,084
So categories, projects, team features, and anything else we add later on will be built on a structure that already understands ownership and access.

106
00:10:58,574 --> 00:11:04,708
Leaving authentication until the end would then just force us to retrofit that logic across the entire app.

107
00:11:05,070 --> 00:11:15,392
So adding it right away after the prototype removes one of the most common sources of rework in AI app development and gives the rest of the build a much safer foundation.

