00:13:24,718 --> 00:13:33,636
So if we add each feature separately without thinking about how they all connect, the AI may create a different structure every single time.

128
00:13:33,902 --> 00:13:41,264
And that can lead to duplicated data, awkward relationships, or features that just work alone fine but do not work well together.

129
00:13:41,774 --> 00:13:50,308
Base44's Discuss Mode just helps us to avoid that problem because it lets us plan with the AI without making any changes to the app.

130
00:13:50,638 --> 00:14:00,944
We can explain what we want to add in the future, ask how the data should be organized, and then review the suggested structure before even sending a build prompt.

131
00:14:01,102 --> 00:14:03,812
So I'm going to open up discuss mode here and use this prompt.

132
00:14:04,174 --> 00:14:09,636
Before I add any new features, I want to plan the full data structure for this task management app.

133
00:14:09,998 --> 00:14:15,172
I want to eventually add categories and team member assignment and project grouping.

134
00:14:15,598 --> 00:14:22,864
Can you help me map out how the data should be structured to support all of these cleanly without needing to be rebuilt?

135
00:14:23,118 --> 00:14:33,184
And then with that, base44 can now think through the relationships between tasks and categories and projects and users and future team assignments without writing any code.

136
00:14:33,264 --> 00:14:39,504
And then we can review the response and then confirm that each task has a clear place in the structure.

137
00:14:39,758 --> 00:14:43,076
Categories can be reused across multiple tasks.

138
00:14:43,598 --> 00:14:51,588
Projects can contain tasks, and team members can eventually be assigned without having to change the entire database later on.

